{
  "name": "screenforge",
  "private": true,
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "license": "AGPL-3.0-or-later",
  "type": "module",
  "engines": {
    "node": "24.x"
  },
  "packageManager": "pnpm@10.26.1",
  "pnpm": {
    "overrides": {
      "@tootallnate/once@>=2.0.0 <2.0.1": "2.0.1",
      "ajv@>=8.0.0 <8.18.0": "8.20.0",
      "js-yaml@>=4.0.0 <4.3.1": "4.3.1",
      "minimatch@>=10.0.0 <10.2.3": "10.2.6",
      "nanoid@>=3.0.0 <3.3.18": "3.3.18",
      "path-to-regexp@>=8.0.0 <8.4.0": "8.4.2",
      "smol-toml@>=1.0.0 <1.6.1": "1.8.0",
      "tar@>=7.0.0 <7.5.21": "7.5.22",
      "undici@>=5.0.0 <6.28.0": "6.28.0"
    }
  },
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "pnpm --filter web run dev",
    "//dev:preprod": "Le même éditeur, branché sur la préproduction, sans toucher au `.env` : une variable posée en ligne l'emporte sur le fichier. Repointer le fichier casserait le mode local-first et la suite e2e qui le vérifie ; l'URL n'est pas un secret, elle part dans le paquet servi.",
    "dev:preprod": "VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://acrobatic-orca-116.eu-west-1.convex.cloud pnpm --filter web run dev",
    "build": "pnpm --filter web run build",
    "preview": "pnpm --filter web run preview",
    "lint": "eslint .",
    "typecheck": "pnpm -r run typecheck",
    "test": "pnpm run test:unit && pnpm run probe:mcp && pnpm run typecheck && pnpm run lint",
    "test:unit": "pnpm -r run test:unit && pnpm run test:publication",
    "test:publication": "node --test scripts/publication-audit.test.mjs",
    "test:e2e": "pnpm --filter web run test:e2e",
    "test:e2e:release": "SCREENFORGE_REQUIRE_CLOUD=1 pnpm --filter web run test:e2e",
    "test:release": "pnpm run format:check && pnpm run audit:publication && pnpm run audit:dependencies && pnpm test && pnpm run build && node scripts/security-headers-audit.mjs --build-only && pnpm run test:e2e:release && pnpm run audit:contrast && pnpm run audit:scale && pnpm run audit:landing",
    "test:release-tag": "node scripts/verify-release-tag.mjs --self-test",
    "verify:release-tag": "node scripts/verify-release-tag.mjs",
    "validate:export": "node scripts/validate-export.mjs",
    "audit:contrast": "node scripts/contrast-audit.mjs",
    "audit:scale": "node scripts/scale-audit.mjs",
    "audit:landing": "node scripts/landing-audit.mjs",
    "audit:dependencies": "pnpm audit --audit-level low",
    "audit:security-headers": "node scripts/security-headers-audit.mjs",
    "audit:publication": "node scripts/publication-audit.mjs tracked",
    "setup:gitleaks": "sh scripts/setup-gitleaks.sh",
    "probe:mcp": "node scripts/mcp-live-probe.mjs",
    "probe:visual": "node scripts/visual-probe.mjs",
    "probe:landing-visuals": "node scripts/landing-visuals.mjs",
    "dev:backend": "pnpm --filter backend run dev",
    "deploy:preprod": "pnpm --filter backend run deploy:preprod",
    "deploy:prod": "pnpm --filter backend run deploy:prod",
    "deploy:ci": "pnpm --filter backend exec convex deploy --typecheck=enable",
    "//convex-cli": "Pas de script pour `convex env|data|run|logs` visant un déploiement du nuage, et c'est mesuré : `--env-file` n'existe que comme option de sous-commande, donc aucun préfixe ne peut l'injecter ; depuis la racine, `pnpm … exec convex … --env-file` le fait lire par pnpm, qui échoue avant d'appeler Convex ; et sourcer le fichier dans l'environnement vise le déploiement **local** sans rien dire, parce que la CLI lit `.env.local` en plus et que son `CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT` l'emporte. Ces commandes se lancent depuis `apps/backend` — `environnements.md` les donne.",
    "format": "prettier --write .",
    "format:check": "prettier --check .",
    "prepare": "husky"
  },
  "lint-staged": {
    "*.{ts,tsx,js,mjs}": [
      "prettier --write",
      "eslint --fix"
    ],
    "*.{css,md,json,html}": [
      "prettier --write"
    ]
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@commitlint/cli": "^21.2.1",
    "@commitlint/config-conventional": "^21.2.0",
    "@eslint/js": "^9.39.5",
    "@playwright/test": "^1.62.1",
    "@types/node": "^24.13.3",
    "@types/react": "^19.2.18",
    "@types/react-dom": "^19.2.4",
    "eslint": "^9.39.5",
    "eslint-config-prettier": "^10.1.8",
    "eslint-plugin-react-hooks": "^7.1.1",
    "eslint-plugin-react-refresh": "^0.5.3",
    "globals": "^17.9.0",
    "husky": "^9.1.7",
    "jszip": "^3.10.1",
    "lint-staged": "^17.3.0",
    "prettier": "^3.9.6",
    "typescript": "^5.9.3",
    "typescript-eslint": "^8.66.0",
    "vercel": "59.1.3"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "convex": "^1.43.0"
  }
}
